{
  "info": {
    "name": "Bluebox MCP server",
    "_postman_id": "6c3f8a2e-4b1d-4f7a-9e5c-2d8b7a1f0c34",
    "description": "Requests for the [Bluebox MCP server](https://docs.bluebox.ai/mcp-server) at `https://app.bluebox.ai/v1/mcp`: JSON-RPC over Streamable HTTP.\n\n**Sign in with OAuth**\n\n1. Send **Setup \u2192 Register the Postman client**. It saves `client_id`.\n2. On the collection's **Authorization** tab, select **Get New Access Token** and sign in to Bluebox in the window that opens.\n3. Send the requests in **Sign in (OAuth)**.\n\n**Use an access token**\n\nWhere a browser can't open, [create an access token](https://docs.bluebox.ai/mcp-server#create-an-access-token), set it as the `access_token` variable and send the requests in **Access token**.\n\n**Variables**\n\nCalls without `workspace_id` use your default workspace. `list_workspaces`, `list_services` and `list_investigations` fill `workspace_id`, `entity_id` and `investigation_id` when they are empty, and `ask` saves `conversation_id`. Empty variables are left out of tool calls.\n\n`ask` starts a Bluebox run that counts against the workspace's daily AI usage. Every other tool only reads.\n",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
